<title>THAILAND: Thai Farmers Bank cuts lending rate.</title>
<headline>Thai Farmers Bank cuts lending rate.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thai Farmers Bank Plc said on Thursday it had cut its Minimum Retail Rate (MRR) by 25 basis points to 13.25 percent with immediate effect.</p>
<p>The reduction of the lending rate would help lower the cost of funds to its best retail clients, the bank said in a statement.</p>
<p>However, the bank's Minimum Lending Rate (MLR) and Minimum Overdraft Rate (MOR) remained unchanged at 13.50 and 13.25 percent respectively, it added.</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642</p>
</text>
